From 71e66f670e0a4ec16b67ff63a18ec2b9064aa21f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Derek J. Clark" <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:16:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 104/206] [FOR-UPSTREAM] HID: hid-msi: Re-init on reset during
 resume

If the USB device is reset while suspended, the USB core restores the
interface and calls the driver's reset_resume callback instead of
resume. hid-msi does not provide one, so the MCU is never re-synced
after such a reset: the deferred cfg_resume work is only scheduled
from msi_resume.

Reuse msi_resume for .reset_resume. It is idempotent and the 500 ms
deferred cfg_resume work re-reads all state from the MCU, which also
covers a device that rebooted across the reset.

Fixes: a9517958e828 ("HID: hid-msi: Add MSI Claw configuration driver")
Cc: stable <stable@vger.kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Derek J. Clark <derekjohn.clark@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-msi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-msi.c b/drivers/hid/hid-msi.c
index f3fe46bf6f41..7b9f72bd54fd 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-msi.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-msi.c
@@ -2107,6 +2107,7 @@ static struct hid_driver msi_driver = {
 	.probe		= msi_probe,
 	.remove		= msi_remove,
 	.resume		= pm_ptr(msi_resume),
+	.reset_resume	= pm_ptr(msi_resume),
 	.suspend	= pm_ptr(msi_suspend),
 };
 module_hid_driver(msi_driver);
